So, my concern is, I don't want to ever be a part of the
Angbandization of NetHack, in the sense that Angband was the
Angbandization of umoria, which is why I recoil reflexively from
suggestions that seem to drag the game into that area of longer,
harder, more detailed, dependent on incredibly rarely generated magic
items, less forgiving (an instadeath after 4 hours from stupidity is
one thing; an instadeath from a missed keystroke after *two weeks* is
another) and so on. The deterministic, "intelligently designed" feel
of NetHack, and the way that it has sustained that very important
distinction between "richly detailed" and "exhaustively detailed" is
what makes it special.

That sermon aside, I think there *is* space in the dungeon for more
special rooms, both in type and quantity, but an increase in special
rooms isn't a valid means to an end for increasing the size of the
main branch of the dungeon. Nor do I think wholesale reshuffling of
the main branch is required or warranted or even a good idea. I mean,
it seems to be Good Enough in many, many ways.



